WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.858
The Department of Defense depends on a broad industrial base to design, build, operate,

00:00:05.858 --> 00:00:07.503
and support mission capabilities.

00:00:07.503 --> 00:00:12.438
Sensitive information often moves across organizational boundaries as many companies contribute to

00:00:12.438 --> 00:00:14.905
the same program or supply chain.

00:00:14.905 --> 00:00:18.606
A weakness at any participant can create wider risk.

00:00:18.606 --> 00:00:23.130
A small supplier may handle information that affects a major platform,

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:27.654
while a service provider may support systems used by several contractors.

00:00:27.654 --> 00:00:30.944
Organization size alone does not determine information sensitivity.

00:00:30.944 --> 00:00:35.468
Cyber threats against the DIB can affect intellectual property, acquisition information,

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:39.169
engineering data, operational capability, cost, schedule, and national security.

00:00:39.169 --> 00:00:44.104
Protecting unclassified information is therefore an important part of protecting defense missions.

00:00:44.104 --> 00:00:46.983
DoD contracts have long included safeguarding requirements,

00:00:46.983 --> 00:00:51.096
including requirements connected to FCI, CUI, and NIST SP 800-171.

00:00:51.096 --> 00:00:55.208
CMMC adds a formal verification framework around applicable cybersecurity expectations.

00:00:55.208 --> 00:01:00.143
Verification helps the government and contracting community distinguish between a stated policy

00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:04.256
and a practice that is implemented within a defined environment.

00:01:04.256 --> 00:01:08.780
It creates common terminology for levels, assessments, findings, affirmations, and status.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.836
CMMC also supports supply-chain accountability.

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:16.593
Requirements may affect subcontractors when protected information or covered contract work flows to them,

00:01:16.593 --> 00:01:21.117
so prime contractors and suppliers need clear communication about information, systems,

00:01:21.117 --> 00:01:21.940
and responsibilities.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:24.818
The program is intended to improve consistency,

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:28.109
but it does not make every contractor identical.

00:01:28.109 --> 00:01:33.044
The required level and assessment type are determined by current program rules

00:01:33.044 --> 00:01:35.511
and the applicable solicitation or contract.

00:01:35.511 --> 00:01:41.680
CMMC cannot eliminate cyber threats or guarantee that an organization will never experience an incident.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:44.559
Its value is stronger implementation, clearer accountability,

00:01:44.559 --> 00:01:48.260
and greater confidence that protected information receives required safeguards.
